WEBVTT

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.480
No, no.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:54.580
America to buy

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.320
some of your horses.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:56.880
In Sous-Jean,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:57.900
we do not sell

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.540
our horses.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.000
We are in a position

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Farewell!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.400
All the money in the world could not tempt us to part with a single one, gentlemen.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.070
For countless ages, the horse has been held sacred by my people.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:15.280
You mean you worship horses?

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.440
They are all sacred.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.340
You worship but one, the black Arabian stallion.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.710
A black Arabian?

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.140
Do you doubt me?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.120
I can hardly blame you.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.000
There is no horse in the world.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:45.570
like him. Come. You will see for yourself. Please. Do you understand now why we worship him of all

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:51.840
horses? He's like a king. He is a king. The living symbol of the horse god of Suzan.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.600
Is it customary to always leave him unguarded in this manner?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.270
Night and day, he's under the constant vigilance of the sacred God.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.390
Wake up! Wake up!

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.780
I show the honor to have you remain as I would get.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.120
Thanks, but our ship is waiting.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.460
May I provide you with an escort for the jungle?

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:25.910
That will not be necessary.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:27.910
It's only a short distance.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.000
I'm going to do it.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.700
But I see it all too.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:04.480
If we can get that black Arabian stallion, it'll mean a fortune for us.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.730
We'd never be able to get away with it, with all those guards on the job.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.720
They'd skin us alive, they caught us.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.060
We'll get Martin to help us.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.760
He'd do anything for a hundred bucks.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:26.080
With the guards, get ready.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.570
Take his place while we tie him up.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.520
Chinzo.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:31.500
Take care of this fellow.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.300
Wheeler and I will get the horse.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:46.350
That black standard is local.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:47.110
Get your horse.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:47.990
He's after us.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:17.730
get out of here. Wait a minute. I know how to get that flag down. What are you going to do? Circle around and run him over the fluke. I'll snag him.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:48.030
The foreigners, they have stolen the god horse, but the gods start for the port.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:49.970
You may still have them all.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:19.610
man was nearby. These friends escaped. Sacred Majesty, I have nothing to do with it. You

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:27.110
have invaded sacred ground. Punishment for this is death. But I tell you I am innocent.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.290
I tried to stop them.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.280
That's the reason they left me lying there in the jungle.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.400
They tried to kill me as I fought for your god horse.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.610
Let me live. I'll bring them back.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:41.340
I swear it.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.680
If the royal guards fail to capture the thieves,

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:49.560
I will give you a chance to earn your liberty.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.680
there'll be another hundred bucks for you

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.540
as soon as I get the horse on shore.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:15.980
That's kind of tough on Wheeler

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.840
having to leave him behind with all those natives.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.660
That's his hard luck.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.110
Maybe we'll pick him up on the next trip.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.790
you sure you can get that black stallion off this boat without any trouble? Absolutely.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.450
When Crawford hears of this wonderful horse, they'll be down on the trailer and nothing

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:55.700
flat. You shouldn't have left Wheeler on that island. He'll have to make trouble for it.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:12:00.000
Don't worry. He'll never leave that island. But you

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.600
never saw a horse like that before.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.340
He's a nice horse, all right.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.060
I've used him in a few polo games, and then I'll groom him for the big show.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.250
It'll be quite a job getting a battle on him.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.020
Never saw a horse yet I couldn't handle.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:23.060
He's a beauty, boss.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.120
Some horse, eh?

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.200
Be careful up now. He's pretty ornery.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.000
that whip. He might have been king in

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.500
too, John, but I'll teach him who's boss around here.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:08.850
Be careful now.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:10.590
He's faster than chain lightning.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:38.950
I told you it was a killer.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.720
He's getting away.

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:43.300
Don't stand there gaping.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:44.820
Get your horses and stop him.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:56.760
Dad.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.640
What do you think? You're a fool!

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:27.330
Yeah, I will.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.410
Where's the father George doing? Dr. Frisales.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.730
There's an officer at the corner, Poland Headquarters.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.990
Tell him to watch the entrance of this alley till I get back, will you?

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:39.450
Sure.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:51.210
I heard you.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.010
I say you're going to help me fool those cops, boy.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:16:00.000
All right, boy.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.960
All right, all right, come on.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.720
Let's the ladies get away.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.040
You won't get far. The radio cars are on the job.

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:59.770
Let's take my car and train them.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.150
Oh, my God.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:36.820
Don't gun it.

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:04.250
Here it is.

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:07.180
That's it, all right.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.930
All right, smart guy.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:13.070
The next time you want to play blind, man, be sure you're smarter than the dog.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:13.780
Come on.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.220
Please let me organize a girl's polo team.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.720
I think it'd be quite a novelty for the Riding Academy.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.730
What do you think of it, Frank?

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.410
She's been pestering me for weeks about it.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.580
I think it's a swell idea, Mr. Bruce.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.000
Dorothy plays a mother.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:06.290
much better game than some men I know. I might have expected that from you. All right, honey.

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:17.910
You win. But I still think it's too rough a game for girls. Where'd that dog come from? I never saw

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:22.860
him around here before. Well, if Jensen doesn't hurry to get back here, he'll find his lunch is gone.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:30.000
Yeah, boy. Well, you're not...

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:40.680
to me are you old boy nobody's going to hurt you oh it's food you want is it well we'll see what

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:54.910
we can do about that good oh you poor dear you must be sobbed there goes jensen's lunch

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:57.950
lousy and dorothy right after the first choker

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.040
All right, honey, you don't want to miss the start of the game.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.270
All right, Dad, coming.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:05.100
Here, help yourself.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.780
I don't think you can through a line.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:30.000
Hey, that's Matt.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:40.850
- Yeah, yeah.

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.990
So you want to play, huh?

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.000
If I catch you around here again, I'll break your neck.

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.240
Keep your shirt on, old man.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:45.500
He's only trying to help you.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:46.920
Maybe he thinks you need another player.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.120
I'd have made that goal if he hadn't stopped the ball.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:50.000
Oh, forget it.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:50.620
We'll give you the goal.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.880
Why, you idiot, why don't you watch where you're going?

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:18.580
Boy, no, no.

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:19.750
Is that your dog?

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:23.820
Yes, but please, Mr. Crawford, he's a good dog and he won't do it anymore.

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:25.150
You bet he won't.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:27.960
And if I see him around there again, I'll have him shot.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:28.260
Yes.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:33.340
